export const prerender = true;
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="BulkUp vs Hevy — Which Workout Tracker Fits How You Train?"
  description="Hevy is a great free gym log with a social feed. BulkUp is built for people who train from a coach's plan: import the PDF, log sets, and track diet too. An honest comparison."
  path="/bulkup-vs-hevy"
  h1="BulkUp vs Hevy: build your log, or import your plan?"
  eyebrow="Comparison"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Hevy</strong> is one of the most popular workout trackers out there — a polished, free
    gym log with routines, progress charts and a social feed. If you build your own routines from
    scratch, it's a strong choice.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>BulkUp</strong> starts from a different place: most people with a coach already
    <em>have</em> a plan — as a PDF or a photo. BulkUp imports that file and turns it into your
    trackable program, then adds the diet side of coaching that pure gym logs skip.
  </p>

  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th></th><th>BulkUp</th><th>Hevy</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Core idea</strong></td><td>Import your coach's existing plan (PDF/photo) and log against it</td><td>Build routines in-app and log them</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Plan import</strong></td><td>PDF or photo, parsed into an editable day-by-day program</td><td>Manual routine builder</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Diet tracking</strong></td><td>Import your nutrition plan; tick off meals and supplements</td><td>Not a focus</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Apple Watch</strong></td><td>Yes — log sets, heart rate and calories from the wrist</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Social</strong></td><td>Private crews: adherence %, streaks with friends</td><td>Public feed, likes and comments</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Platforms</strong></td><td>iOS + Apple Watch</td><td>iOS, Android, web</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Status</strong></td><td>Pre-launch — waitlist open, founder pricing</td><td>Available now, free tier</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Pick Hevy if…</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You design your own routines and want a free, proven logger today.</li>
    <li>You want a public social feed and Android or web access.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Pick BulkUp if…</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your coach hands you a plan as a PDF, photo or spreadsheet and you're tired of copying it by hand.</li>
    <li>You want training <em>and</em> diet from that plan in one app.</li>
    <li>You'd rather compete on adherence with your own crew than post to a feed.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    BulkUp launches soon on iOS. Join the <a href="#waitlist">waitlist</a> below — it's free and
    locks in founder pricing.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
